id: pm-tqel
title: "Consolidate history commands: history-redact/history-repair/history-compact/activity/restore under pm history subcommands"
description: "pm history <id> stays the default view; history-redact -> pm history redact, history-repair -> pm history repair, history-compact -> pm history compact, activity -> pm history activity, restore -> pm history restore (old spellings aliased). Duplicate check: no existing history-namespace item; history feature items are all closed deliverables."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:history",simplification
created_at: "2026-07-05T04:53:05.215Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-07T11:33:25.565Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-07T11:33:24.944Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-07T11:33:24.944Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: pm history gains redact/repair/compact/activity/restore subcommands with flag parity; old top-level spellings alias-shimmed with identical output; default pm history <id> view unchanged; contracts/MCP/completions/docs regenerated; existing history-* specs pass via aliases
parent: pm-n7rr
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Native history redact/repair/compact/activity/restore share SDK behavior with permanent aliases and consistent contracts, addressing, output, recovery and completion. Legacy maintenance loads only its mutation family; Fish includes unbounded activity; exact-token tests and purpose documentation strengthen the contract."
expected_result: Agent-friendly native discovery preserves existing flags/output/default history view and avoids unnecessary legacy startup work.
actual_result: "All 8537 tests in 637 files passed with exact 100/100/100/100. Both linked tests, zero-violation tracked static gates, all 74 touched named function docstrings, and installed npm/Bun 15-step CLI plus SDK journeys passed. First-round bot artifacts acknowledged individually; updated-head CI and re-review requested before merge."
