comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-07T09:09:45.812Z","harness:codex","Implementation scope: history redact/repair/compact/activity/restore share existing SDK behavior with permanent legacy aliases, unchanged default history view, discoverable contracts and completion parity. Prerequisites pm-0z7n and pm-hb7ug8 read live with their implementation evidence. Delivery shares pm-34w8za maintenance substrate. Test first, preserve existing command outputs and error contracts."
  "2026-09-07T09:46:00.939Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: shared stream snapshot and verified maintenance pipeline integrated with redact/repair/compact and restore drift checks. Native history commands share registrations with permanent root aliases; runtime flags, output envelopes, addressing, SDK/MCP discovery and completion resolve the selected operation. Focused maintenance and namespace suites passed; full coverage and type gates are running."
  "2026-09-07T09:50:05.412Z","harness:codex","Graph evidence: full all-status graph audit covered 2653 items and 13062 directed edges with no omitted fields, missing targets, ordering cycles, isolated items or degree-one items; all active and terminal non-outcome items reach an outcome through typed relationships. Execution graph has 12 layers and the knowledge graph is one connected component. Seven historical hierarchy divergences remain informational under the existing historical policy. Added verifies edges for the maintenance substrate and permanent alias guarantees exercised by this delivery. GitHub secret-scanning and Dependabot open-alert reads both returned empty arrays."
  "2026-09-07T10:17:31.429Z","harness:codex","Installed candidate acceptance passed independently under npm and Bun using the packed working-tree artifact: create/update, redaction preview and apply with canary removal verified in raw history bytes, restore, compaction, repeated full-chain verification, repair preview, native/legacy activity equality, named history addressing, native flag contracts, and public SDK export execution. Both executables resolved inside their isolated installation roots. This is candidate-artifact evidence, distinct from the already-published daily version. GitHub open Dependabot, code-scanning and secret-scanning inventories remain empty; repository secret scan passed."
  "2026-09-07T10:22:38.239Z","harness:codex","Distribution verification: scheduled Auto Release run 34095818006 completed successfully on 2026-09-07 and public v2026.9.7 is a non-draft stable release. Anonymous exact-version npm metadata, npx and bunx explicit/default CLI dispatch, MCP stdio and HTTP discovery (Skills and Apps), all declared bin coverage, and executor negative controls passed. Exact public npm and Bun installed agent sessions each passed 11 bounded steps. These prove the existing immutable daily release; this branch remains the next eligible release candidate. The broader packed-candidate npx/bunx smoke also passed with 13 packages and TypeScript consumer validation."
  "2026-09-07T10:32:23.962Z","harness:codex","TDD follow-up: the exact coverage run passed all 8533 tests but exposed unvisited native parsing branches. Added real bootstrap normalization and canonical contract selection cases. A new restore completion arity test failed because raw flag metadata lacks explicit boolean types; Zsh and Fish now consume the shared enriched invocation contract, keeping --force/--json valueless and --author/--message/--pm-path value-taking. All 115 targeted completion and contract tests passed. Regenerated the refusal census from SDK contracts after native probe identity normalization. Full coverage and the remaining static chain are rerunning without threshold or exclusion changes."
  "2026-09-07T10:38:29.044Z","harness:codex",All 8536 tests passed; exact coverage found one obsolete startsWith(history-) summary fallback after every supported legacy history command moved to explicit alias contracts. Removed the unreachable heuristic instead of inventing a command solely to execute it. Coverage and contract verification will be rerun on this final source.
  "2026-09-07T10:48:12.547Z","harness:codex","Final local verification passed: all 8536 tests across 636 files with exact 100/100/100/100 and zero uncovered counts. Linked namespace/completion/grammar tests passed. Final build and the full static command chain passed across resumed runs, including an isolated rerun of timing-sensitive gates. Native and compatibility flag/output parity, default history addressing, permanent aliases, SDK exports and installed npm/Bun workflows are verified. Latest pm-changelog 2026.9.6 is installed; generated notes will be reviewed with this delivery. Existing review inventory/watch/acknowledgement tooling will cover every bot artifact and edited revision before merge."
  "2026-09-07T10:51:08.852Z","harness:codex","Post-closure tracker validation: all 2653 item streams checked with zero history drift, missing/unreadable streams, chain/hash mismatches, version skew or workspace-state mismatches. Resolution validation retains 295 historical incomplete structured-close records, matching the initial all-status corpus; both delivered items include complete immutable resolution/expected/actual evidence. Changelog check passed using pm-changelog 2026.9.6; repository secret scan passed. No tracked work remains in progress."
  "2026-09-07T11:13:29.893Z","harness:codex","CI follow-up: the tracked-file static gate now includes the newly added registration module and reports one CodeFactor complexity excess (17 versus 16). Earlier local assurance ran before new files were staged, so that pass did not establish the tracked-file scan for the final tree. Direct reproduction confirms the finding; simplify repeated option string checks with the existing shared decoder, stage new files before final static verification, and rerun exact coverage. Sentry/public release evidence remains separate."
  "2026-09-07T11:18:43.915Z","harness:codex","Completed CodeRabbit review has four valid findings: generated release-note wording, omitted Fish activity --unbounded, legacy maintenance registration family overloading, and a substring-only salvage-tail assertion. Implement all four plus the CI complexity correction in one follow-up commit. Direct static scan reports 100 percent module/export/member docstrings; additionally document every touched named internal helper so the broader diff-based review is actionable. Greptile CLI reports exhausted free quota and Sourcery declined the diff size; neither is an approval."
  "2026-09-07T11:32:58.477Z","harness:codex","Review fixes verified: final rebuilt source passed all 8537 tests in 637 files with exact 100/100/100/100 and zero uncovered counts. Both linked commands passed. Final tracked-file static scan covers 1262 files with zero complexity violations and 100 percent module/export/member docstrings; all 74 touched named functions have purpose docstrings. ESLint, duplication, contracts, public SDK snapshots, generated surfaces and secret scan passed. Installed npm and Bun candidate journeys each passed 15 CLI steps plus public SDK execution. Every first-round bot artifact has a revision-specific reaction and response, with all four findings acknowledged inline."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-07T10:43:15.815Z","harness:codex","Nested commands need one semantic operation mapping across parsing, item addressing, universal output, contracts, activation and completion. Completion must consume enriched takes_value metadata rather than infer boolean arity from optional raw schema fields."
  "2026-09-07T11:21:19.637Z","harness:codex",Stage newly created source files before running gates that enumerate git-tracked paths. A working-tree lint pass and a tracked-file static assurance pass can cover different file populations until the new paths enter the index.
